  "about": "The price list the grocery screen pulls. One entry per thing you buy. 'foods' maps ingredients in js/foods.js to this item: the number is how many grams to buy for each gram a recipe uses (raw for cooked meat, dry for cooked rice, whole can for drained beans, with the peel for bananas). 'typical' is a typical price, not any store's price; a price you record in the app replaces it at that store. 'src' says where a typical price comes from (see 'sources') and 'note' adds a line about it. Prices are in dollars. Units: oz, lb, g, kg, fl oz, ml, L, gal, count, or 'per lb' for food sold by weight. 'gPerMl' lets sizes in fl oz work; 'each' is the grams in one piece, so sizes in 'count' work. A store's 'brand' is the name of its main store brand: a price recorded under that name counts as the store's own product, and the app mentions it as a pointer, never as a promise that every item comes in it. 'fresh' marks food sold loose or unbranded. 'check' marks packaged foods that more often carry nut warnings. 'keeps' marks food that stays in stock until the meals use it up; pantry and frozen items keep unless told otherwise. After editing, run: node tools/check-plan.mjs",
